# TASK-260715-3f4lxy handoff evidence — focused rework 01

## Outcome

Implemented the reviewer-requested fail-closed delta while preserving the accepted macOS provider-only scope.

- Recursive prohibited-field detection now uses case/punctuation normalization with a bounded prohibited-root and fixed semantic-suffix policy. Nested regression fixtures cover private-key material/data, passphrase bytes, password value, seed bytes, decrypted private key, staging credential payload, raw host-key data, and key-byte payload variants.
- The superseded profile-reference expectation was replaced by an exact five-field versioned start request carrying configuration generation plus the lowercase SHA-256 digest of the exact canonical stored snapshot bytes.
- A present request must match both stored generation and exact-byte digest before first capture or returns `profileGenerationMismatch`. Nil start options remain allowed. A fresh-loader regression proves same-generation account replacement is rejected.
- No App Group, Keychain, secret-bearing model, route, network, packet-forwarding, or profile-write path was added. The shared core remains candidate-neutral.

## Validation with real exit codes

- Accepted contract SHA-256 recomputation — exit 0; matched `8c81d2dc15904d6648f1333620370ac2c8c455e081fe6e98b4480a92c64bd5f2`.
- Final `swift test --filter SSHProfileSnapshotLoaderTests` — exit 0; 13/13 passed.
- Combined loader/runtime-start/session focused run — exit 0; 52 tests passed.
- Full `swift test` — exit 0; 392 tests in 32 suites passed, including the complete HEV suites. No HEV failure occurred in this final rework run.
- `swift build` — exit 0.
- `swift format lint --recursive Sources Tests Package.swift` — exit 0 with no diagnostics.
- `make check-core-boundaries` — exit 0; dependency and import boundaries valid.
- `git diff --check -- Sources Tests LOGBOOK.md` — exit 0.
- Loader prohibited-API boundary scan — exit 0 and clean.
- Secret model-field scan — exit 0 and clean.

One intermediate focused run exited 1 after the implementation compiled: two uppercase top-level privacy fixtures were rejected earlier as noncanonical JSON ordering and therefore produced `profileCorrupt` instead of the intended prohibited-field error. The fixtures were moved to canonical nested single-key positions while retaining case/punctuation coverage; the final focused and full-suite runs above are green.

## Board validation

`task-board validate` process exit 0 and reported one existing aggregate issue: `STORY-260715-2wjwuf` is stored as `to-dev` while its child aggregate is `development`. Board files were not edited directly. This does not affect task code or the developer handoff.

## Contract trace

The updated task-scoped schema evidence is attached as `TASK-260715-3f4lxy_schema.md`. The implementation/rework decision and final 392-test HEV-inclusive result are recorded in `LOGBOOK.md`.
