8:### 1736 — macOS provider captures one complete non-secret SSH profile generation (TASK-260715-3f4lxy)
9-- IMPLEMENTATION: `SSHProfileSnapshotV1` now carries the accepted complete profile, canonical endpoint, credential reference/generation, ordered host-key policy, and trust history as immutable value types. A strict deterministic JSON pass enforces UTF-8, sorted keys, canonical strings/numbers, no insignificant whitespace, duplicate rejection, depth 8, exact v1 envelope headers, recursive prohibited-field names, and exhaustive field invariants before exposing the model.
10-- DECISION: The 4096-byte bound is checked over the actual binary-property-list representation of the exact three-key `providerConfiguration`, so owner and manager-contract metadata count toward the NetworkExtension envelope. The macOS adapter reads only `NETunnelProviderProtocol.providerConfiguration`; it has no App Group, Keychain, route, network, packet, or profile-write path.
11:- GENERATION SAFETY: A fresh `SSHProfileRuntimeSnapshotLoader` owns one runtime start. A present exact five-field v1 start request binds `configurationGeneration` to the SHA-256 digest of the exact stored canonical snapshot bytes before first capture; nil options may capture the validated stored value. Byte-identical rereads return the original capture, while stale requests, same-generation field replacement, newer-generation replacement, and concurrent competing captures fail with the fixed privacy-safe `profileGenerationMismatch` error.
12-- PRIVACY REWORK: The recursive field scan applies case/punctuation normalization plus a bounded prohibited-root/fixed-suffix policy. Nested fixtures cover `privateKeyMaterial`, `privateKeyData`, `passphraseBytes`, `passwordValue`, `seedBytes`, `decryptedPrivateKey`, `stagingCredentialPayload`, raw-host-key data, and key-byte payload variants.
13-- VERIFICATION: Thirteen focused loader tests, 52 combined loader/runtime-start/session tests, and the complete 392-test/32-suite run pass, including HEV. `swift build`, recursive format lint, core-boundary validation, and `git diff --check` all exit 0.
